[h1]Taoist — v6.0.01[/h1]
A [b]hardcore rework[/b] of the base game: a living world, a harsh economy, towns you can rule, families, lifelong storylines and tougher battles.
Most features can be tuned or turned off in [b]S&M Configs[/b] (title screen; page 3 holds the optional features). The harder your settings, the higher your S&M score and the better your rewards. If it gets too hard, combine it with other mods.
Give me a like to let me know it is useful, thanks! If you want to support the work: [url=https://ko-fi.com/fouru]Ko-fi[/url]

[h2]⚠ Requirements[/h2]
[list]
[*][url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3385996759]Fouru's ModLib[/url] v2.2.34 or newer
[*][b]Move ModLib to the TOP of your mod list[/b], then [b]restart the game[/b].
[/list]

[h2]New game[/h2]
[list]
[*]Starting divine artifacts at character creation (Bagua Jade, Eye of Providence, Devil Demon Pot, any combination)
[*]Option to skip the intro and the first battle
[*]Roles for the player and NPCs: Power, Speed, Tao, Atk, Def, Angel, Evil, Merchant (each with its own advantages)
[*]Prioritized destiny level, S&M difficulty presets (Level 0-10), one-life mode, in-game trainer
[/list]

[h2]S&M score[/h2]
[list]
[*]Every S&M setting is worth points (P): harder settings raise the score, easier ones lower it
[*]The score changes battle exp and loot (-20% to +50%), gives a title (Leisurely Wanderer, Mortal Path, Seeker of the Dao, Ascetic, Asura, Heaven Defier) and a start bonus for a new save
[*]Score records of every character across your saves (Taoist Settings)
[/list]

[h2]Storylines[/h2]
[list]
[*]12 NPC storylines with portraits, real battles and several endings:
Cold Sword, Old Huang's Debt, Exploding Furnace, Sworn Brothers, Granny's Herb Garden, Red Lotus (the final battle),
and the long lines: Hundred-Year Wager, Roadside Inn (both over a hundred years), Sealed Tomb, Cursed Disciple, Thunder Remnant and Heart Demon (opening at higher realms)
[*]Each line has several acts, time limits and fail branches. Late or failed acts open a different path instead of ending the line, and the lines remember how the others ended
[*]Scenes drawn for every step (caves, tombs, storms, inns, battlefields...), and a quest per open line in the Mission window
[*]Granny Shi's herb garden on the world map: a seclusion place for long cultivation
[/list]

[h2]World and NPCs[/h2]
[list]
[*]NPCs grow, level up their skills, craft artifacts, and earn roles and titles
[*]Teams: hire NPCs (monthly pay), friends join for free, and members who fight beside you grow closer. Members may also betray you
[*]NPCs join your battles: enemies, friends, sect members, town guards
[*]Stalkers follow you after you show rare items. Fight them or pay them off
[*]Random encounters with choices and rewards: wounded cultivator, chess hermit, hooded peddler, collapsed cave, spirit beast cub, town festival, and a rare heavenly trial for high scores
[*]Reworked dramas with several lines per situation and new choices
[*]Quests: slice-of-life, challenge master, commissions (ask NPCs to find items for you)
[*]NPCs find their own fortunes and ancient inheritances (rarely)
[/list]

[h2]Families and legacy[/h2]
[list]
[*]NPCs take dao companions (same-sex option) and have children who join the world at 16
[*]Your household: monthly upkeep, gifts from your family, and a family accounts window; your family tree on the game's kinship screen
[*]When your character dies, play on as your grown-up child or grandchild and keep the legacy: items, spirit stones, techniques (S&M option)
[/list]

[h2]Economy[/h2]
[list]
[*]Prices rise over time (inflation, currency reform), with sales and price hikes in June and December
[*]Buying and selling in towns costs extra
[*]Bank accounts and storage fees. Unpaid fees lock your storage
[*]Bank loans at 3%/month, due in 12 months. Overdue debts bring reminder letters, then debt collectors (pay, hand over goods, or fight). Beat them twice and the bank writes off the debt but blacklists you
[*]Player market with NPCs: list items, negotiate (spirit stones or barter), VIP market, recent deal prices, and buy orders filled by the townspeople (a table with count, price, town and months left)
[*]Exchange items for sect contribution
[/list]

[h2]Towns[/h2]
[list]
[*]Town budgets and taxes (with monthly tax statistics), town masters and guardians
[*]Bounties: town masters post wanted notices and hunters chase the targets (you included). Hunt the wanted yourself from the bounty board
[/list]

[h2]Cultivation[/h2]
[list]
[*]Seclusion and enlightenment lasting years (spirit veins, ancient inheritances, heart demons, time rifts...) while the world keeps living
[*]Qi cultivation, cultivation with spirit stones, natural breakthroughs
[*]Rebirth to level 1 and cultivate again with better basic stats
[*]Time skips simulate every month of the world, with a progress window
[/list]

[h2]Battle and growth[/h2]
[list]
[*]Mana shields for players, NPCs and monsters, special monsters, monsters that grow stronger over time
[*]Reworked damage and defense, with block, evade and crit rules
[*][b]Damage Calc[/b] window (battle button, player info or F9): your attack and defense numbers step by step, the last hits dealt and taken, and the last foes you fought compared with you
[*]Exp and stats grow through battles. Level-ups are harder. Skills and artifacts gain expertise
[*]Losing a battle can cost exp, items, spirit stones, lifespan, or your character (one-life mode). The Resurrection Pill and rings protect you
[*]Refine rings, outfits, artifacts and mounts: refine levels and random adjustment slots by quality (slot n unlocks at level n x 100). Unlocked slots can be rerolled
[*]Several divine artifacts at once, a hotkey for each one, and repair of damaged artifacts
[/list]

[h2]Interface[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Taoist Settings[/b] (in the game settings): damage multiplier, notifications, encounters, hotkeys, score records
[*][b]Taoist log[/b]: taxes, fees, deals, loans, bounties and encounters, month by month
[*]Icons for spirit stones, stats and items in the mod's texts
[*]Optional: hide the map and unit count in battle, hide training and skill previews
[*]Languages: English, Chinese (Simplified and Traditional), Korean, Japanese, Vietnamese, Thai, Russian, German, French, Spanish and Latin, plus a custom language system
[/list]

[h2]Open source[/h2]
You can use my ModLib to make your own mod: [url=https://github.com/4azuo/GuiGuBaHuang-ModLib/]https://github.com/4azuo/GuiGuBaHuang-ModLib/[/url]

